.TH "EPX\-API" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-api \- send requests to any Emporix API path
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx api [flags]
epx api [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx api delete"
Send DELETE to an API path and print the JSON response.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx api delete PATH [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sends DELETE to PATH on the configured API host, with the JSON body that \fB\-\-file\fR gives (none without it), and prints the response body as JSON (YAML with \fB\-o yaml\fR) with sorted keys and every value as sent (nothing for an empty one). {tenant} in PATH is replaced with the tenant; query values given with \fB\-p\fR replace inline ones. It sends no other header, such as the Content\-Language that the Unit Service requires to create or update a unit.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type PATH at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requests only the scopes given with \fB\-\-scope\fR besides the tenant: name every write scope that the endpoint needs, as Emporix grants only requested scopes.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p, \-\-param <key=value>\fR
Query parameter as key=value (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-scope <strings>\fR
OAuth scope to request besides the tenant (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx api delete /product/{tenant}/products/100200 \-\-scope product.product_manage \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx api get"
GET an API path and print the JSON response.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx api get PATH [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sends GET to PATH on the configured API host and prints the response body as JSON (YAML with \fB\-o yaml\fR) with sorted keys and every value as sent. {tenant} in PATH is replaced with the tenant; Accept\-Language: * requests every translation. Query values given with \fB\-p\fR replace inline ones. Request every scope the endpoint needs with \fB\-\-scope\fR: Emporix grants only requested scopes and may silently omit data otherwise.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p, \-\-param <key=value>\fR
Query parameter as key=value (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-scope <strings>\fR
OAuth scope to request besides the tenant (repeatable).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx api get /site/{tenant}/sites
epx api get /product/{tenant}/products \-p pageSize=5 \-\-scope product.product_read_unpublished
.fi
.RE
